import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 637 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 638 | 2026-10-23 | **Pitch review, build A (her 20:44 request; 21:17: '샵', and yes to the new order).** Two independent reviewers walked all 66 Pitch lessons in en/ko; this build fixes the blocking items. (1) Keyboards: the ScKeys crop now ends on a white-key edge and half-cut black keys at the edge are not drawn (the 'clipped keyboard' at 390 and 900); From staff to keys uses 2 octaves round the clef instead of 4 (keys were 6 px), 8va 2 octaves with C labels, Low and high 3 octaves. (2) Feedback: Scales and Modes lines turn red when wrong and green when right (were navy); Key signatures wrong KEY taps now say what was tapped and where to look (were silent); the sharp/flat word row is hidden while she taps; Accidentals rules and 'accidental or key signature?' tries hide the note names and bands until a miss or the answer (the neighbours gave the answer away); tonic-triad question no longer prints the note names. (3) Terms app-wide: 샵 (not 샤프), 반음/온음 (not 반 걸음), 산호색 (not 코랄), 옥타브 (not 완전8도), 오선 (not 스태프) on the staff buttons, half/whole step in Scales; Korean copula and particles after note names; 높은 음, 낮은 음 (was 높이와 낮이); 느껴져요 typo; Korean wrong-answer hints no longer quote the English mnemonics. (4) Order of the Pitch concepts: Keys and staff, Accidentals, Intervals, Scales, Key signatures, Chords, Modes. (5) Lessons are numbered straight through the groups on the Home, and the intervals, chords and keyboard-patterns drill levels show that lesson number and a short name, sorted in lesson order; the intervals group buttons open the matching level. Smaller: 'Tap any key in a group of 2', middle C 'near the middle', 1 half step (not steps), inversion questions show a keyboard. Patch sc/patch660.py on the t659 build (it re-splices sc/kq.jsx, sc/iv.jsx, sc/ch.jsx). Build B next: intervals and chords by keys in between (her method), four kinds of triad, 7th chords, V7, 7th-chord inversions. Still open from the review: Accidentals, Key signatures and Modes onto KqEngine and cutting their repeated steps; moving the Scales fingering lessons; one keyboard everywhere. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
